From fac92012d52ac769cc43757dff1ac1cc913d36d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chen Cheng <85005591+ischencheng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:59:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] [Perf][Kernel] Add a BF16x3 router GEMM for fp32 router
 weights on Hopper

On SM90, GateLinear runs fp32 router weights above 32 tokens as
F.linear(x.float(), w), an fp32 SGEMM on CUDA cores. SM100 has a CuteDSL
BF16x3 kernel for this and gfx950 a hipBLASLt one; SM90 had none.

Add a Triton kernel that splits each fp32 weight tile into three bf16
terms in registers, runs them on bf16 tensor cores, and adds the
tensor-core partial of every K-tile into an fp32 accumulator. Small
batches split K and sum the partials in a fixed order. Configs come from
a fixed table by token bucket and router shape, with no autotuning.

GateLinear reaches it through the existing BF16x3 tier on SM90. Batches
of 32 or fewer tokens keep the fp32 GEMV, and VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT keeps
the existing path. The kernel test runs in a new H100 Buildkite step.

Signed-off-by: Chen Cheng <85005591+ischencheng@users.noreply.github.com>
