From c53179a49216b0a238200453d95bfff075e55d9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chen Cheng <85005591+ischencheng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:53:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Rewrite the SM90 BF16x3 router GEMM in CuteDSL

Replace the Triton kernel with a CuteDSL kernel next to the SM100 one, as
router GEMMs in this tree are written in CuteDSL.

The MMA runs swapped (64 experts as the wgmma M, tokens as N). TMA brings
the fp32 weight and bf16 token tiles to shared memory. The MMA warpgroup
splits each k16 slice of its fp32 weight fragment into three bf16 terms
in registers and issues register-A wgmma; the next slice is split while
the current one runs. First-term products are promoted into an fp32
register accumulator every K-tile; the much smaller second and third
terms keep their own partial over K, as on SM100. Split-K sums the
partial tiles of a thread-block cluster through DSMEM in rank order, so
it needs no second kernel or workspace.

Tiles and split-K come from a small cost model (fewest waves times the
per-CTA time) fitted on H200. The kernel is a VllmCuTeDSLJitKernel that
GateLinear registers for startup warmup, so warmup compiles from fake
tensors instead of launching.

