From b2b3383a7cb58d57c59a902d49d7a5893ae88c35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chen Cheng <85005591+ischencheng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:29:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Use the fp32 router kernel up to 24 tokens on SM90

On H200 the BF16x3 kernel is flat at 6-10 us while the fp32 kernel grows
with the token count, so the crossover is at 18-28 tokens depending on the
shape. Keep the GB200 rule for (5120, 256) Blackwell-only: on H200 it ran
40 and 48 tokens on the fp32 kernel at 11.9 and 13.8 us instead of 7.6 us.

Also cover the Beam-1.0 and Muse Spark Open router shapes in the tests.

Signed-off-by: Chen Cheng <85005591+ischencheng@users.noreply.github.com>
---
